{"author":"John Wesley","book":"Notes on the Bible","chapter":767,"classification":{"bucket":"Christian Classics / Commentaries","canonicalStatus":"noncanonical","contentKind":"commentary","cautionReason":"","doctrinalStatus":"historical","labels":["christian-classics","commentaries"],"severity":0},"id":"classics:wesley:Ps.30","lineage":[],"metadata":{"author":"John Wesley","authorshipDateRange":"18th century","genre":"Commentaries","tradition":"Methodist","translator":null,"edition":"CCEL edition; source omits 2 Samuel 24","rights":"Public Domain","source":{"id":"wesley","provider":"CCEL","sourceUrl":"https://www.ccel.org/ccel/wesley/notes.html","title":"Notes on the Bible"}},"originalBook":"Psalms","sourceVolumeId":"wesley","source":{"id":"wesley","sourceUrl":"https://www.ccel.org/ccel/wesley/notes.html","title":"Notes on the Bible"},"title":"Psalms 30","reference":"Psalms 30","notes":[],"verses":[{"verse":1,"text":"He praises God for delivering him, and exhorts others to praise him, ver.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":2,"text":"1-5.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":3,"text":"Recollects his former security, and his prayer when in trouble, ver.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":4,"text":"6-10.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":5,"text":"And stirs himself up to thankfulness, ver.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":6,"text":"11, 12.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":7,"text":"A Psalm and song, at the dedication of the house of David.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":8,"text":"Title of the psalm.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":9,"text":"Song - A psalm to be sung with the voice to an instrument.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":10,"text":"David - At the dedication of David's house, which was built, 2 Sam. v, 11, and doubtless was dedicated, as God had commanded.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":11,"text":"5.","sourceParagraph":2,"scriptureVerseStart":5,"scriptureVerseEnd":5},{"verse":12,"text":"Cometh - Speedily and in due season.","sourceParagraph":2,"scriptureVerseStart":5,"scriptureVerseEnd":5},{"verse":13,"text":"7.","sourceParagraph":3,"scriptureVerseStart":7,"scriptureVerseEnd":7},{"verse":14,"text":"Mountain - My kingdom: kingdoms are usually called mountains in prophetical writings.","sourceParagraph":3,"scriptureVerseStart":7,"scriptureVerseEnd":7},{"verse":15,"text":"9.","sourceParagraph":4,"scriptureVerseStart":9,"scriptureVerseEnd":9},{"verse":16,"text":"Profit - What wilt thou gain by it?","sourceParagraph":4,"scriptureVerseStart":9,"scriptureVerseEnd":9},{"verse":17,"text":"The dust - Shall they that are dead celebrate thy goodness in the land of the living?","sourceParagraph":4,"scriptureVerseStart":9,"scriptureVerseEnd":9},{"verse":18,"text":"Or, shall my dust praise thee?","sourceParagraph":4,"scriptureVerseStart":9,"scriptureVerseEnd":9},{"verse":19,"text":"11.","sourceParagraph":5,"scriptureVerseStart":11,"scriptureVerseEnd":11},{"verse":20,"text":"Sackcloth - Given me occasion to put off that sackcloth, which they used to wear in times of mourning, Esth iv, 1 chap. xxxv, 13 Isaiah xxxii, 11 Joel i, 13.","sourceParagraph":5,"scriptureVerseStart":11,"scriptureVerseEnd":11},{"verse":21,"text":"Girded - With joy, as with a garment, surrounding me on every side.","sourceParagraph":5,"scriptureVerseStart":11,"scriptureVerseEnd":11},{"verse":22,"text":"12.","sourceParagraph":6,"scriptureVerseStart":12,"scriptureVerseEnd":12},{"verse":23,"text":"My glory - My tongue.","sourceParagraph":6,"scriptureVerseStart":12,"scriptureVerseEnd":12}],"scriptureReference":{"book":"Psalms","chapter":30}}